{"name":"Gale Force","hex":"#35454e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gale force","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Of a wind, having the speed and strength of a gale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gale_force"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gale Force","blocks":[{"text":"Gale Force is a 2002 action thriller starring Treat Williams and co-starring Michael Dudikoff, Curtis Armstrong, Susan Walters, Tim Thomerson, Marcia Strassman, and many more. It was directed by Jim Wynorski."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6d/Gale_Force_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gale_Force","wikidata":"Q3765027"},{"title":"Beaufort scale","blocks":[{"text":"The Beaufort scale is an empirical measure that relates wind speed to observed conditions at sea or on land. Its full name is the Beaufort wind force scale. It was devised in 1805 by Francis Beaufort, a hydrographer in the British Royal Navy. It was officially adopted by the Royal Navy and later spread internationally."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Beaufort_scale_12_notext.jpg/330px-Beaufort_scale_12_notext.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaufort_scale","wikidata":"Q170464"},{"title":"Gale","blocks":[{"text":"A gale is a strong wind; the word is typically used as a descriptor in nautical contexts. The U.S. National Weather Service defines a gale as sustained surface wind moving at a speed between 34 and 47 knots. Forecasters typically issue gale warnings when winds of this strength are expected. In the United States, a gale warning is specifically a maritime warning; the land-based equivalent in National Weather Service warning products is a wind advisory."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Brooklyn_Museum_-_After_a_Gale--Wreckers_-_James_Hamilton_-_overall.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_After_a_Gale--Wreckers_-_James_Hamilton_-_overall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gale","wikidata":"Q2144546"},{"title":"Force","blocks":[{"text":"In physics, a force is an action that can cause an object to change its velocity or its shape, or to resist other forces, or to cause changes of pressure in a fluid. In mechanics, force makes ideas like pushing or pulling mathematically precise. Because the magnitude and direction of a force are both important, force is a vector quantity. The SI unit of force is the newton (N), and force is often represented by the symbol F."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Force_examples.svg/330px-Force_examples.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Force","wikidata":"Q11402"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/FrancisBeaufort.jpg/500px-FrancisBeaufort.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/FrancisBeaufort.jpg/500px-FrancisBeaufort.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sir Francis Beaufort","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrancisBeaufort.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Beaufort_wind_scale.png/500px-Beaufort_wind_scale.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Beaufort_wind_scale.png/500px-Beaufort_wind_scale.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Data graphic showing Beaufort wind force in scale units, knots and metres per second","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeaufort_wind_scale.png"},{"srcset":"h